⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the "ONE user-cancel rendering" invariant already has an exception — the manual `/compact` cancel window**

The new helper's doc declares itself the single user-cancel rendering "shared by the compaction cancel windows", but a third compaction-cancel window in the same library still renders the same receipt through the raw idiom — `_runManualCompact` in `lib/src/cli/agent_cli_compaction.dart:722`:

```dart
} on CancelledException {
  // Compaction-ONLY interrupt (issue #1085 round-2 review): Ctrl+C
  // during a bare /compact stops the compaction, not the session —
  // a dim receipt, no `error:` line, the REPL keeps working.
  io.writeln(_style.dim('compaction interrupted'));
}
```

Output is byte-identical today, so nothing breaks — but this is the *original* user-cancel window (#1085 round-2), and any future change to cancel rendering (pane routing in TUI mode, receipt dedup, styling) will silently miss `/compact` exactly the way this PR's helper was introduced to prevent.

Suggested fix (one line):

```dart
} on CancelledException {
  _renderUserCancel('compaction interrupted');
}
```

Either migrate the third site or soften the doc comment to name only the three gh-1929 windows, so the stated invariant matches the code.

